; fish-base vertex: O = incenter of triangle abd, sitting ON the ac-diagonal.
; A′ (2026-07-18): the diagonal's continuation O→c is collinear with the given
; a-ray — a constructible completion, so it is STATED as a fourth element
; (`--ray & .c`) rather than derived. The statement is EVEN (the two bisectors
; plus both halves of the diagonal) with no emergent at all; derive now yields
; genuinely-new lines only, so the old odd 3-ray form no longer produces this
; fold. The four rays place in ONE position class (placements depend only on
; ray LINES), but three distinct min-mountain M/V patterns survive there
; (spine-M, d-bisector-M, b-bisector-M). Under the approved rule (2026-07-19,
; .superpowers/sdd/diagnosis-spine-m.md) {toward} selects sides/mirrors, never
; M/V — so the pattern is PINNED explicitly (`--ray & .c mountain`, the spine),
; leaving only the two mirror sectors. `{toward .b}` (this file) and its sibling
; `{toward .d}` then pick the two MIRROR realizations: same face count, same
; table positions, opposite layer order — not the same fold twice, the whole
; point of this slice.
;
; `.bel` assertions have no vocabulary for stacking/rank (see
; tests/test_bel_assert.ml's `assertion` type), so `faces = 6` is all this
; file can pin; the actual DIFFERENCE (this file's rank vs. -toward-d.bel's)
; is pinned by tests/test_flatten.ml's
; test_flatten_derive_opposite_ray_fish_base, which reads Fold_state.rank
; directly and asserts the two runs disagree.

paper square

mark --diag = map .a onto .c
mark --ray = through .a .c

step left
mark --l1 = map --ab onto --diag
mark --l2 = map --da onto --diag
flatten (--l1) (--l2) (--ray & .a) (--ray & .c mountain) {toward .b}

; assert faces = 6
